{
  "description": "Validation fixtures of the import pipeline, run by supabase/tests/0017_import_validation.test.sql. Each case is one import as the planner of organization A: the parent files (optional) are staged and sealed first, then the case file; expected lists every error and warning of the import as (file_no, row_no, column_name, code, level), where file_no defaults to the case file (the last one) and row_no 0 means the whole file. value, value_length and detail are compared when given. The source_missing warning that every sealed file gets (no originals are uploaded) is left out. columns are the contract columns the file maps; each row has one cell per column, a string, or {\"repeat\": s, \"times\": n}, or {\"today_plus\": n} (YYYY-MM-DD; current_date + n while the demand partitions reach past tomorrow, otherwise counted back from their end, so 1 is always the last accepted day).",
  "seed": "Organization A: calendars CAL-A (SA, observes public holidays) and CAL-NOCTRY (no country, does not observe); a SA closure 2026-03-20..2026-03-22; locations LOC-A1 (central) and LOC-A2 (branch, parent LOC-A1); brand BR-A; items P-1 (introduced 2024-01-01), P-2 (discontinued 2025-01-01), P-3 and P/4; supersession P-2 -> P-3; supplier SUP-A (lead times 10/20); supplier items SUP-A/P-1 (lead 10, p90 20) and SUP-A/P-2 (lead 10, no p90); demand P-1/LOC-A1 on 2024-07-15. Organization B: brand BR-B-ONLY, item P-B-ONLY, location LOC-B-ONLY.",
